    "display_name": "Hello to You",
    "long_instructions": "You’re building your chatbot and want it to say hello to the user by name. For example, if your name is “Grace,” the chatbot might say “Hello, Grace!”\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n1. Set the value of the `name` variable to someone’s name.\r\n2. Print a message that greets the user and mentions their name.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo print text that includes a variable, you can use a Python formatted string. A formatted string starts with the letter `f` and can print a variable by surrounding it in curly braces.\r\n\r\nFor example, the following Python code will print “My name is” followed by the value of the `first_name` variable:\r\n\r\n```\r\nprint(f\"My name is {first_name}\")\r\n```",
